WEBVTT

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:01.580
Your build failed.

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:02.586
Again.

00:00:04.550 --> 00:00:06.062
So you open the log.

00:00:06.550 --> 00:00:08.834
And it just... keeps... going.

00:00:09.350 --> 00:00:11.458
Somewhere in here is the reason.

00:00:12.930 --> 00:00:13.960
Flaky test?

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:14.916
Cache?

00:00:16.080 --> 00:00:17.160
Cosmic rays?

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:18.190
Rerun.

00:00:18.270 --> 00:00:19.170
Hope.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:20.366
Repeat.

00:00:22.150 --> 00:00:24.485
Or... you could follow the paper trail.

00:00:25.850 --> 00:00:27.312
Meet Tracewise.

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:29.586
It reads the failed run,

00:00:30.000 --> 00:00:31.847
pulls out the lines that matter,

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:33.999
checks the code at that commit,

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.080
and what changed in your push.

00:00:36.500 --> 00:00:37.560
Read-only.

00:00:37.600 --> 00:00:39.720
Every claim comes with a receipt.

00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:42.837
Then it writes up what it found,

00:00:43.250 --> 00:00:44.698
and how sure it is.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.878
Evidence. Not guesses.

00:00:49.500 --> 00:00:51.050
Not enough evidence?

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.421
It says so.

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:56.810
Tracewise.

00:00:56.850 --> 00:00:58.110
Trace failures.

00:00:58.150 --> 00:00:59.511
Find answers.

00:01:02.500 --> 00:01:03.894
See how it works.
